Subject: [PATCH] Keep the OCTA private CTRL port out of sequencer bridges

JACK's ALSA sequencer bridge otherwise opens both raw-MIDI subdevices,
preventing the control panel from opening its exclusive CTRL connection.
Only the second subdevice of the OCTA base/EXP IDs is private. Normal
DIN MIDI capabilities and direct raw-MIDI CTRL access remain available.

---
--- a/sound/usb/midi.c
+++ b/sound/usb/midi.c
@@ -1811,6 +1811,12 @@
 	struct snd_usb_midi *umidi = rmidi->private_data;
 	struct port_info *port_info;
 
+	/* CTRL is a private protocol endpoint, never a generic sequencer port. */
+	if (number == 1 && (umidi->usb_id == USB_ID(0x0582, 0x0120) ||
+			    umidi->usb_id == USB_ID(0x0582, 0x0121))) {
+		seq_port_info->capability = SNDRV_SEQ_PORT_CAP_NO_EXPORT;
+		return;
+	}
 	/* TODO: read port flags from descriptors */
 	port_info = find_port_info(umidi, number);
 	if (port_info) {
